[{:db/id 17592186192677 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-26e02fce-e08e-5fe6-a3ec-6ad998577401"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-26e02fce-e08e-5fe6-a3ec-6ad998577401" :question/id #uuid "26e02fce-e08e-5fe6-a3ec-6ad998577401" :question/math-academy-id "q-90448" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Give your answer rounded to two decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-1, & 2<x<3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{12}, & 3\\le x<4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{4}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-1)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{4}x\\cdot \\frac{5}{12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}-x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{5x}{12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})|}_{2}^{3}+{\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{24}|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{16}+\\frac{35}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{145}{48} \\\\  & ≈3.02,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nrounded to two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aded4a40-1d18-5fec-bc4b-4bcb36ab2d42"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aded4a40-1d18-5fec-bc4b-4bcb36ab2d42" :answer-field/id #uuid "aded4a40-1d18-5fec-bc4b-4bcb36ab2d42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6b109b1d-9413-505f-ad96-a041eb6ca00e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e329b197-e48b-55a0-8164-4bc46b1e5644" "answer-e4dba7f7-2146-5ff3-a626-ce33b04b8a0b" "answer-01b4f1c9-6a5b-52c7-aa2b-f725b7d61594" "answer-6b109b1d-9413-505f-ad96-a041eb6ca00e" "answer-3cd6386a-9b90-5c4e-be0a-bdee4537678d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e329b197-e48b-55a0-8164-4bc46b1e5644" :answer/id #uuid "e329b197-e48b-55a0-8164-4bc46b1e5644" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4dba7f7-2146-5ff3-a626-ce33b04b8a0b" :answer/id #uuid "e4dba7f7-2146-5ff3-a626-ce33b04b8a0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01b4f1c9-6a5b-52c7-aa2b-f725b7d61594" :answer/id #uuid "01b4f1c9-6a5b-52c7-aa2b-f725b7d61594" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.87" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b109b1d-9413-505f-ad96-a041eb6ca00e" :answer/id #uuid "6b109b1d-9413-505f-ad96-a041eb6ca00e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.02" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cd6386a-9b90-5c4e-be0a-bdee4537678d" :answer/id #uuid "3cd6386a-9b90-5c4e-be0a-bdee4537678d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.54" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192676 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3743ef7f-fa52-55af-8a67-99557ea6f27d" "question-c64c8376-4f9a-5df0-81b9-bf811d12f7ce" "question-edac9b93-8284-5302-bc8b-9583d4ecc8f3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3743ef7f-fa52-55af-8a67-99557ea6f27d" :question/id #uuid "3743ef7f-fa52-55af-8a67-99557ea6f27d" :question/math-academy-id "q-131154" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[2e-(e-1)X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{e}{e{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}},\\,1<x<e\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[2e-(e-1)X]=2e-(e-1)\\text{E}[X]\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot \\frac{e}{e{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{e}{ex-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{e-1}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{e}{e-1}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{e-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2e-(e-1)X] & =2e-(e-1)\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & =2e-(e-1)\\cdot \\frac{e}{e-1} \\\\  & =2e-e \\\\  & =e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-40bc13bb-3a56-5bb3-8230-e9e5cf644479"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-40bc13bb-3a56-5bb3-8230-e9e5cf644479" :answer-field/id #uuid "40bc13bb-3a56-5bb3-8230-e9e5cf644479" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c85412a1-0e83-564f-8a9b-83a321c6575e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d7fa3a08-2b65-5156-aae1-9ccac58678b5" "answer-e8914a7c-ea0f-5a3e-bdf9-4afc9ee04ada" "answer-77138f44-7002-5bb8-ac6c-cc59e24ef477" "answer-c85412a1-0e83-564f-8a9b-83a321c6575e" "answer-990d8356-79d6-5c6b-8d72-fd39fd724f7e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7fa3a08-2b65-5156-aae1-9ccac58678b5" :answer/id #uuid "d7fa3a08-2b65-5156-aae1-9ccac58678b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8914a7c-ea0f-5a3e-bdf9-4afc9ee04ada" :answer/id #uuid "e8914a7c-ea0f-5a3e-bdf9-4afc9ee04ada" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77138f44-7002-5bb8-ac6c-cc59e24ef477" :answer/id #uuid "77138f44-7002-5bb8-ac6c-cc59e24ef477" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3e-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c85412a1-0e83-564f-8a9b-83a321c6575e" :answer/id #uuid "c85412a1-0e83-564f-8a9b-83a321c6575e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-990d8356-79d6-5c6b-8d72-fd39fd724f7e" :answer/id #uuid "990d8356-79d6-5c6b-8d72-fd39fd724f7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c64c8376-4f9a-5df0-81b9-bf811d12f7ce" :question/id #uuid "c64c8376-4f9a-5df0-81b9-bf811d12f7ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-152904" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[4X+2].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}, & 0<x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of the expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[4X+2]=4\\text{E}[X]+2\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8})|}_{0}^{1}+{(-\\frac{1}{2x})|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{8}-0)+(0-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[4X+2] & =4\\text{E}[X]+2 \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{7}{8}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76d69cbc-7ea6-5219-b9fe-b27e60e2aa63"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76d69cbc-7ea6-5219-b9fe-b27e60e2aa63" :answer-field/id #uuid "76d69cbc-7ea6-5219-b9fe-b27e60e2aa63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-12065d32-e113-5992-bb8d-f535e75fb9ea" :answer-field/choices ["answer-12065d32-e113-5992-bb8d-f535e75fb9ea" "answer-b73c6eb0-be0e-57a4-8c3b-4e4f51c6378c" "answer-18efb766-1d3d-58da-bff5-d24f02292777" "answer-29173ece-c32d-5596-a3a8-34d0349c05ed" "answer-a2a8b51a-6b08-55ab-89b7-ef577ff59874"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12065d32-e113-5992-bb8d-f535e75fb9ea" :answer/id #uuid "12065d32-e113-5992-bb8d-f535e75fb9ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b73c6eb0-be0e-57a4-8c3b-4e4f51c6378c" :answer/id #uuid "b73c6eb0-be0e-57a4-8c3b-4e4f51c6378c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18efb766-1d3d-58da-bff5-d24f02292777" :answer/id #uuid "18efb766-1d3d-58da-bff5-d24f02292777" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29173ece-c32d-5596-a3a8-34d0349c05ed" :answer/id #uuid "29173ece-c32d-5596-a3a8-34d0349c05ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2a8b51a-6b08-55ab-89b7-ef577ff59874" :answer/id #uuid "a2a8b51a-6b08-55ab-89b7-ef577ff59874" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-edac9b93-8284-5302-bc8b-9583d4ecc8f3" :question/id #uuid "edac9b93-8284-5302-bc8b-9583d4ecc8f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-152907" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[12X-8].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}, & 0<x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{8}{9}, & 1\\le x<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of the expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[12X-8]=12\\text{E}[X]-8\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{8}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8x}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{12})|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{9}|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{12}-0)+(\\frac{16}{9}-\\frac{4}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}+\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[12X-8] & =12\\text{E}[X]-8 \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\frac{17}{12}-8 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a9112695-ad08-5300-a06c-ea0b770acb45"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a9112695-ad08-5300-a06c-ea0b770acb45" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9112695-ad08-5300-a06c-ea0b770acb45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-30945d0b-c228-50cd-9399-4fc6759027b5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-52eacba8-2ac3-5a25-85fe-9c675a072c68" "answer-c10ec2db-f24e-557d-8a16-961d2cfcd677" "answer-30945d0b-c228-50cd-9399-4fc6759027b5" "answer-5ffc82d5-d3b0-5643-95db-cbc049b36c70" "answer-477a366f-5027-5734-8066-1c5b19a5ae4a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52eacba8-2ac3-5a25-85fe-9c675a072c68" :answer/id #uuid "52eacba8-2ac3-5a25-85fe-9c675a072c68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/v